0 300px; min-width: 50%;"><div class=3D"css-4pmh08"><div class=3D"markdown-=
body"><p>Airwallex uses versioning to improve our API contracts without aff=
ecting existing users.</p>
<p>When we need to introduce a backwards-incompatible change, such as renam=
ing or splitting a field, we will create a new date version which clients c=
an migrate to when ready.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">What is the latest version?</h4><p>The latest version =
is <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">2026-05-29</code>.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">Which version am I using?</h4><p>Your version is store=
d in your account and automatically applied to your API calls.</p>
<p>Please <a href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/app/login?redirectToDocs=3Dt=
rue" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;"=
>log in</a> to view your version.</p>
<p>You may override this version on a per call basis by setting the <code s=
tyle=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">x-api-version</code> header.  This should only be used in exceptional c=
ases, such as when testing and migrating to a newer version, or when callin=
g on behalf of another account.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">How do I upgrade to a new version?</h4><p>Refer to the=
 Changelog to learn about the contract changes introduced in the new versio=
n. You can also view the full documentation for a selected version using th=
e <strong>Version</strong> drop-down menu in the sidebar.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">Testing and Development</h4><p>Set the <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">x-api-version</code> header to the new version on the affected endpoint=
s. Modify your code according to the new API contracts.</p>
<p>Test the changes in our sandbox environment without affecting live data.=
 You may also use feature flagging to incrementally migrate traffic. For de=
tails, see <a href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/docs/developer-tools__sandb=
ox-environment-overview" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflo=
w-wrap: break-word;">Sandbox environment overview</a>. </p>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">Switch to production</h4><p>Once your production traff=
ic is migrated to the new version via the <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">x-api-version</code> header, notify our support team. We will update yo=
ur account to the new version. Shortly (&gt; 1 hour) after this, you may re=
move the <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">x-api-version</code> header from your API calls.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">How does Airwallex define "backwards-compatible" and "=
backwards-incompatible"?</h4><p>The following are examples of backwards-com=
patible changes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Adding new API endpoints</li>
<li>Adding new optional fields to request models</li>
<li>Adding new fields to response models</li>
<li>Adding new required fields to request models where the change relates t=
o a new payment corridor or method</li>
<li>Modifying content of unstructured text fields, such as error messages a=
nd field labels</li>
</ul>
<p>We regularly introduce such backwards-compatible changes to our API to s=
upport new product features.  These should not affect existing integrations=
 so we can introduce them directly to all versions.  This avoids clients ha=
ving to upgrade to a newer version to utilise the new functionality.  Pleas=
e ensure your integration supports these changes, e.g. disable checks on  u=
nknown fields in the response.</p>
<p>Changes other than these may be either of the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>Backwards-incompatible change: these are changes to our API contracts w=
hich we can use versioning to avoid existing client impact.</li>
<li>External data requirement change: see question below.</li>
</ul>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">What's an "external data requirement change"?</h4><p>O=
ccasionally, regulators or third-party service providers may mandate additi=
onal data requirements for existing functionality.  In these cases we will =
need to enforce the requirement for all clients who use the affected functi=
onality.  To minimise impact, we will likely introduce the third-party chan=
ge requirement to all versions (to avoid needing to do a large upgrade to l=
atest version).  This situation has not yet arisen; if/when it does we will=
 be in contact with full details.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-weight: 800; font-size: 16px; margin-block-end: 8px; marg=
in-block-start: 8px">Why do the API URLs include "/v1"?</h4><p>The URL vers=
ion is expected to stay as "v1" for the foreseeable future.  However, it ma=
y be used at a later date for a complete API overhaul, such as migrating RE=
ST to GraphQL.</p>
