;"><div class=3D"markdown-body"><p>The <strong>Airwallex OAuth 2.0 API</str=
ong> allows your applications to access other Airwallex clients' resources =
on behalf of the client by implementing the <a href=3D"https://datatracker.=
ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6749" target=3D"_blank" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-=
weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">OAuth 2.0 protocol</a>. Airwallex =
currently supports the <strong>authorization code</strong> grant type using=
 the standard <a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6749#sect=
ion-4.1" target=3D"_blank" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overf=
low-wrap: break-word;">authorization code flow</a> and the <a href=3D"https=
://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7636" target=3D"_blank" style=3D"color:=
 #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">Proof Key for Code =
Exchange (PKCE) extension</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Airwallex OAuth 2.0 API</strong> consists of two endpoints:</p>
<ol>
<li>An <a href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/docs/api/issuing/transactions#/=
Authentication/OAuth2/_oauth_authorize/get" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-w=
eight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">authorization</a> endpoint for obta=
ining the <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">authorization_code</code>.</li>
<li>A <a href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/docs/api/issuing/transactions#/A=
uthentication/OAuth2/_oauth_token/post" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weigh=
t: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">token</a> endpoint for exchanging the <=
code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">authorization_code</code> or <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">refresh_token</code> for an <strong>access token</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Once an <strong>access token</strong> is obtained, you may call the Airw=
allex APIs on behalf of the client by setting the Authorization header in e=
very API request (e.g. <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">Authorization: Bearer &lt;access token&gt;</code>). Only the APIs corre=
sponding to the <a href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/docs/developer-tools/p=
artner-connections/oauth-scopes" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500;=
 overflow-wrap: break-word;">scopes</a> set in the <a href=3D"https://www.a=
irwallex.com/docs/api/issuing/transactions#/Authentication/OAuth2/_oauth_au=
thorize/get" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: brea=
k-word;">authorization</a> request will be allowed access. To use the <stro=
ng>Airwallex OAuth 2.0 API</strong>, you will need to register your applica=
tion by contacting <a href=3D"mailto:strategic-partnerships@airwallex.com" =
style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">stra=
tegic-partnerships@airwallex.com</a>. The <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">client_id</code> and <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">client_secret</code> are issued upon successful registration.</p>
