s=3D"markdown-body"><p>Partner Webhooks API allows OAuth applications to re=
ceive real-time events originating from OAuth-authorized Airwallex accounts=
.</p>
<p>To receive webhook events on behalf of your users, first create a Webhoo=
k for your OAuth application and connect the target OAuth-authorized accoun=
t to it. The types of events you can receive are limited by the <a href=3D"=
https://www.airwallex.com/docs/developer-tools/partner-connections/oauth-sc=
opes" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;=
">Scopes</a> set out in the OAuth authorization. During the consent flow, u=
sers will authorize your application for listening to their webhook events.=
</p>
<p>Partner Webhooks API requires <a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/do=
c/html/rfc7617" target=3D"_blank" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500=
; overflow-wrap: break-word;">HTTP Basic authorization</a> for OAuth applic=
ations. The HTTP header must include <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">Authorization: Basic [token]</code> where <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">token</code> is a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base64" styl=
e=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">Base64</=
a> encoded string of <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">[client_id]:[client_secret]</code>. The <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">client_id</code> and <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">client_secret</code> are issued by Airwallex for your OAuth application=
.</p>
