><div data-radium=3D"true" style=3D"margin-top: 32px;"><div class=3D"markdo=
wn-body"><p>A <strong>FundsSplit</strong> will guide you through the proces=
s to divide part of the collected funds to another destination before settl=
ing to the account that owns the funds.<br><br>You may create multiple <str=
ong>FundsSplits</strong> for the same source of funds to send money to diff=
erent destinations. However, one <strong>FundsSplit</strong> will only have=
 one destination.<br><br>You may specify the following on a FundsSplit.</p>
<ol>
<li>What is the source of funds? Denoted by <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">source_type</code>.</li>
<li>How much do you want to split? Denoted by <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">amount</code>.</li>
<li>Who will receive the funds? Denoted by <code style=3D"
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: #2f2529;
    background-color: hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid hsla(0, 0%, 60%, 0.1);
    font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  ">destination</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Currently, FundsSplit only works when the source of funds is a payment a=
cceptance transaction, and the destinations are connected accounts to the f=
unds owner.<br><br>Data Retention Policy: You can query and operate FundsSp=
lit resources for a maximum of 2 years since creation.</p>
