<p>All card schemes publish account range information which helps understan=
d the product, issuer country code,=20
issuer name etc. Hence, merchants can request account range data under a pa=
rticular PAN thereby enabling=20
business logic such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>Merchants query for BIN info using the PAN to get information about car=
d type so that they can surcharge=20
if the card used is commercial / credit or other cases.</li>
<li>Merchants would like to know the brand and product information to run d=
iscounts and offers on the website.=20
The cart amount will be dynamically updated to reflect the discounted price=
.</li>
<li>Merchants query on the card details like country code to run some risk =
level checks at their side without=20
depending on the acquirer. Merchants may not want to accept cards issued in=
 a certain country, because sending=20
this to the acquirer may cost them additional charges (gateway fee / author=
ization fee, etc.).</li>
</ul>
