s you to manage terminals, including creating, retrieving, updating, activa=
ting, deactivating, terminating, and processing payment intents in terminal=
s. <br><br>A Terminal can be in one of the following states: </p>
<ol>
<li><strong>ACTIVE</strong>: The Terminal is activated and ready to use. </=
li>
<li><strong>INACTIVE</strong>: The Terminal is deactivated for any reason. =
</li>
<li><strong>TERMINATED</strong>: The Terminal is terminated and can't be us=
ed anymore.</li>
</ol>
