div><div data-radium=3D"true" style=3D"margin-top: 32px;"><div class=3D"mar=
kdown-body"><p>Platforms must share PSP Settlement Split information with A=
irwallex before funds settle to the holding account, by calling the <a href=
=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/docs/api/issuing/transactions#/Scale/PSP_Sett=
lement_Splits/_api_v1_psp_settlement_intents__psp_settlement_intent_id__spl=
it/post" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-wo=
rd;">Split a PSP Settlement Intent API</a>. This data typically originates =
from the pay-in PSP's reporting feed.</p>
<p>Funds in the holding account are inaccessible to all parties until the f=
unds are released to other connected accounts. A Platform can choose to <a =
href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/docs/api/issuing/transactions#Scale/PSP_S=
ettlement_Splits/_api_v1_psp_settlement_splits__id__release/post" style=3D"=
color: #612FFF; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">release a PSP=
 Settlement Split</a> anytime. On release, funds are transferred to a conne=
cted account for the recipient, such as a seller.</p>
<p>If a Platform wants to apply a transaction fee to the seller, they can c=
reate one split for the amount due to the seller, and can create another sp=
lit for the fee to the platform's own account.
A Platform can trigger a <a href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com/docs/api/issu=
ing/transactions#/Payouts/Payments/Intro" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-wei=
ght: 500; overflow-wrap: break-word;">payout</a> from any connected account=
 to an <strong>external bank account</strong> at any time (for example, at =
the end of a payout cycle).
PSP Settlement Splits form part of the <a href=3D"https://www.airwallex.com=
/docs/scale__psp-agnostic-solution" style=3D"color: #612FFF; font-weight: 5=
00; overflow-wrap: break-word;">PSP-agnostic payout solution</a>.</p>
